Q: C++ Pass a reference to an array to function A: <p>It should be noted that a C++ reference is not a pointer.</p>
<pre><code>int test(int(&amp;arr)[5])
 {
  return sizeof(arr)/sizeof(int);
 }
</code></pre>
<p>Will return 5, because the array does NOT decay to a pointer to the first element.</p>
